  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a twenty-one-song set at the Evanston SPACE in Evanston, Illinois, on Tuesday, August 24, 2021 [1][2]. This evening was the 312th show by the band captured in the Internet Archive’s collection, following a performance at the Pabst Theater the previous day [2]. The recording, titled tmg2021-08-24, was taped and transferred by Liz Hamilton [1]. The setlist begins with “(We Belong Together)” and “Aulon Raid” before moving into “Cry for Judas” and “Tallahassee” [1]. Tracks like “You or Your Memory” and “Pez Dorado” follow, leading to “Tollund Man” and “Tidal Wave” [1]. The show features a notable bustout of “Snow Owl,” which had not appeared in 61 archived shows or 1,359 days, making it a mythic rarity with only two archived performances [1][2]. Another rare moment occurs with “Against Agamemnon,” a bustout from 188 archived shows and 4,906 days, with only three archived performances [1][2]. The set continues with “Cobscook Bay,” “Southwestern Territory,” “The Diaz Brothers,” “Wolf Count,” “Game Shows Touch Our Lives,” “Getting Into Knives,” and “Up the Wolves” [1]. The encore includes “The Slow Parts on Death Metal Albums,” “Song for Dennis Brown,” “Broom People,” and “This Year” [1]. The full recording runs 96 minutes [1].",
